    "traits": {
      "value": [
        {
          "resource_id": "monster_trait",
          "stats": {
            "trait_name": {
              "value": "Eternal Damnation"
            },
            "trait_description": {
              "value": "(divine, necromancy)\n\nAs long as its soul chain remains intact, a forge-spurned can't be truly destroyed. It rises again fully healed at the next sundown, even if its physical body was destroyed."
            },
            "id": "9174c9f4-78ba-4239-a0f8-51a80257e594",
            "updated_at": {
              "value": "2026-03-17T12:41:22.444580"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "resource_id": "monster_trait",
          "stats": {
            "trait_name": {
              "value": "Searing Heat"
            },
            "trait_description": {
              "value": "(fire)\n\nA creature that touches a forge-spurned (including by grappling it or hitting it with an unarmed attack) takes 2d6 fire damage with a DC 21 basic Reflex save."
            },
            "id": "4cb11f94-4d44-43b9-b385-ff7c3ed9b4c2",
            "updated_at": {
              "value": "2026-03-17T12:41:22.444580"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "resource_id": "monster_trait",
          "stats": {
            "trait_name": {
              "value": "Soul Chain"
            },
            "trait_description": {
              "value": "(divine, fire, necromancy)\n\nIf a creature is slain by an attack from the soul chain and the forge-spurned is able to retain the creature's corpse, it can bind the creature's soul into the soul chain (as bind soul) with a day of work at a forge and a successful DC 20 Crafting check. An individual whose soul is bound in this way can't be resurrected unless the soul chain is destroyed (Hardness 5, HP 20, BT 10)."
            },
            "id": "ac53bebc-404b-4c55-bd40-a5352fc15e55",
            "updated_at": {
              "value": "2026-03-17T12:41:22.444580"
            }
          }
        }
