        {
          "resource_id": "monster_action",
          "stats": {
            "action_name": {
              "value": "Forge Breath"
            },
            "action_description": {
              "value": "(divine, evocation, fire)\n\nThe forge-spurned breathes a cloud of stinging soot, ash, and glowing embers. This can affect either a 30-foot cone or a 20-foot burst centered on the forge-spurned and persists for 1d4 rounds. Each creature that moves into or starts their turn in the area takes 6d6 fire damage, with a DC 21 basic Reflex save. A creature that fails its save is also blinded for 1 minute. Creatures within the cloud are concealed, though not from the forge-spurned. The forge-spurned can't use Forge Breath again until it has used Inflate Bellows."
            },
